Fixed. The bug was on line 7 of `src/import_merge.ts`: the duplicate check compared URLs case-sensitively (`b.url === inc.url`), so a hostname differing only in case (`https://EXAMPLE.com/a` vs `https://example.com/a`) wasn't matched and got added as a second entry.

Change: compare via the existing `normalizeUrl` helper (which lowercases the hostname) instead of raw string equality:

```ts
const match = result.find((b) => normalizeUrl(b.url) === normalizeUrl(inc.url));
```

Verified:
- Case-differing URL now merges into the existing entry (1 entry), tags unioned (`["x","y"]`).
- Non-matching URLs still append unchanged.
- `deno check` and `deno test` both pass (3/3 tests).


